2026-08-16 22:34:57 [INFO   ] main:   parasitic_fraction     ST=0.9914
2026-08-16 22:34:57 [INFO   ] main:   regen_effectiveness    ST=0.0013
2026-08-16 22:34:57 [INFO   ] main:   mu0H_max_T             ST=0.0000
2026-08-16 22:34:57 [INFO   ] main:   fluid_mdot_kgs         ST=0.0000
2026-08-16 22:34:57 [INFO   ] main:   frequency_Hz           ST=0.0000
2026-08-16 22:34:57 [INFO   ] main: Interpretation:
2026-08-16 22:34:57 [INFO   ] main: mu0H_max, frequency and fluid_mdot show ~0 sensitivity because the
2026-08-16 22:34:57 [INFO   ] main: current amr_cycle.py model structure makes COP_electrical algebraically
2026-08-16 22:34:57 [INFO   ] main: independent of Qc: COP_electrical = 1 / [(Th/Tc-1)/eta_2nd_law(eps) +
2026-08-16 22:34:57 [INFO   ] main: parasitic_fraction], since both W_mag and W_parasitic scale linearly
2026-08-16 22:34:57 [INFO   ] main: with Qc and cancel. Field/frequency/flow rate DO change how much cooling
2026-08-16 22:34:57 [INFO   ] main: you get (Qc, via dTad) but NOT, in this model, how efficiently you get it.
2026-08-16 22:34:57 [INFO   ] main: Real AMR systems don't have this decoupling -- eddy-current losses scale
2026-08-16 22:34:57 [INFO   ] main: with frequency^2, viscous dissipation with mdot^2, and magnet support/
2026-08-16 22:34:57 [INFO   ] main: motor sizing with field -- so eta_2nd_law and parasitic_fraction should
2026-08-16 22:34:57 [INFO   ] main: be state-dependent functions rather than constants. The
2026-08-16 22:34:57 [INFO   ] main: state-dependent formulation implemented in loss_model.py
2026-08-16 22:34:57 [INFO   ] main: addresses this limitation.
